From 4de0b6d17795c3388835d5ec287ce293f793abc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:12:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] ci(release): what was built is tried on a fresh Mac, as a
 download, before it can reach the releases page

The Release workflow gets a job between build and publish. On a Mac that has built nothing, scripts/mac-shell/check-download.sh takes the files of the release
as a person who downloads them would: checksums, signature, both programs for both kinds of Mac from macOS 14 on, no library but the system's; marked as a
browser marks a download, macOS refuses the app, in the words the install page and the notes of that very release quote; the road through
System Settings is followed as far as a script can, to the dialog that wants an administrator's password; with the mark taken off Arbor starts,
says its version, shows its welcome window and waits; given the permission as System Settings gives it, the process that waited runs, docks
two windows side by side, quits, and both are back in view at their own sizes; the disk image holds the same app, its signature whole.

The release is built with the Swift of the newest Xcode on the runner that is no beta: Apple's compiler for what people run, and no path into a
toolchain in the runner's home folder in the programs.
---
 .github/workflows/release.yml       |  46 +++-
 scripts/mac-shell/announce.swift    |  13 ++
 scripts/mac-shell/check-download.sh | 322 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 373 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 scripts/mac-shell/announce.swift
 create mode 100755 scripts/mac-shell/check-download.sh

