+# Builds a release on GitHub's Mac, tries it on another as a person who downloads it would, and leaves it on the releases page as a
+# DRAFT for a person to read and publish: the disk image, the zip, their checksums, the Homebrew cask, and notes from the top of CHANGELOG.md.
 # It starts by hand and in no other way (Actions → Release → Run workflow, or `gh workflow run release.yml -f rehearsal=false`), on a branch
 # or on a tag: v0.9.0 for the version in the VERSION file, v0.9.0-rc.1 for a release candidate of it. See "Making a
 # release" in docs/INSTALL.md. Pushing a tag starts nothing: a tag marks a commit, and marking one must not take half an
@@ -50,12 +50,13 @@ jobs:
